{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06HF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-formal-objects-yoneda}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:09cb624634d57f425d2526f59926e98beac689424e0a4e57b1dc4d394e6c680a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5f9090a9c7f525b5c6b72bb684db0cd81b174523e6a2c77e9a6df3704a522b67", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLater we are interested in producing smooth morphisms from\nprorepresentable functors to predeformation categories <MATH_0001>.\nBy the discussion in\nRemark <REF_0001>\nthese morphisms correspond to certain formal objects of <MATH_0002>.\nMore precisely, these are the so-called versal formal objects of <MATH_0003>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1fb6f900db2fef825c6d4f295c4a179aece8516c9a9184127644cee69486b74d", "unit_id": "tag:06HF:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "06HF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\xi$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$R \\in \\Ob(\\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\xi$", "MATH_0006": "$\\underline{\\xi}: \\underline{R}|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-formal-objects-yoneda}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-versal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dbcfb42d6a7648218efa63bbda37cd1d15964e984e319143058991db41516c25", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1cfa043a90da25380d70d7d85f42e5e6e0adfdb000afcd87a9a0ad3fdda42cb8", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category cofibered in groupoids.  Let <MATH_0002> be a formal\nobject of <MATH_0003> lying over <MATH_0004>.\nWe say <MATH_0005> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>versal<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if the corresponding morphism\n<MATH_0006>\nof Remark <REF_0001> is smooth.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ba7388a2f1d881fe423eb30ab769eea7526e34e61e035e01a03708f770e2a1d1", "unit_id": "tag:06HR:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "06HF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal\nC_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$\\xi$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\xi$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n& y \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\xi \\ar[r] & x\n}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$\\widehat{\\mathcal{F}}$", "MATH_0008": "$y \\to x$", "MATH_0009": "$B \\to A$", "MATH_0010": "$\\xi \\to y$", "MATH_0011": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n& y \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\xi \\ar[r] \\ar[ur] & x\n}\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$\\xi$", "MATH_0013": "$\\underline{\\xi} : \\underline{R}|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-formal-objects-yoneda}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-versal-object}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:34e155d9d02c5499b06b47010c7fe9af0ceac47b70243d9e22fbed6aecd7de63", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dd8254ba477254eaf5714c7bbb52a2b34b099b88820bcf0ce7ffabe03c0d5ead", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category cofibered in groupoids over <MATH_0002>, and let <MATH_0003> be a formal object of <MATH_0004>.  It follows\nfrom the definition of smoothness that versality of <MATH_0005> is equivalent to the\nfollowing condition: If\n<MATH_0006>\nis a diagram in <MATH_0007> such that <MATH_0008> lies over a\nsurjective map <MATH_0009> of Artinian rings (we may assume it is a small\nextension),  then there exists a morphism <MATH_0010> such that\n<MATH_0011>\ncommutes. In particular, the condition that <MATH_0012> be versal does not depend on\nthe choices of pushforwards made in the construction of\n<MATH_0013> in\nRemark <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:437ef198705ad8d48151f7ee353adc0cf569120c3914c2785e9aef62426b1dbe", "unit_id": "tag:06HS:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06HF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\xi$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\eta$", "MATH_0005": "$\\widehat{\\mathcal{F}}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\xi \\to \\eta$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-versal-object-quasi-initial}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ac0c1681681832fe805a23cbf101d8a841b7adaed7f7903ed2f20f920d6ff50a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:aafe0b1e42700a77cd351902e8d7a9bc016aaedd916e05a602986f52f9a4413a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a predeformation category.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a versal formal object of <MATH_0003>.\nFor any formal object <MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005>,\nthere exists a morphism <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:37ece39ceae2015a43dafe437821d539eb54ddf7d72f1b400eba28ef72a8e3f5", "unit_id": "tag:06HT:statement"}
